  "scope": [
    "Audit the English, Japanese, and Traditional Chinese README files for Temple-specific commands, concepts, profiles, paths, and lifecycle vocabulary that appear without a human-facing explanation.",
    "Add one human-facing Core Skills guide and one concise Temple terminology guide; link README first-use concepts to those guides without linking beginners directly to agent-facing SKILL.md contracts.",
    "Add one localized engineering-style delivery-path diagram to the request-flow section while keeping the README a compact two-diagram entry point.",
    "Preserve WI-0077 and WI-0079 work, avoid optional dependencies and external diagram vendors, and do not commit or push without separate authorization."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "All three READMEs keep the same information hierarchy and link every invoked Temple Core Skill to a matching human-facing explanation.",
    "The terminology guide distinguishes Temple-specific names from ordinary software terms and explains authority boundaries in plain language.",
    "The localized delivery-path diagrams use one geometry, remain readable at desktop and narrow widths, and do not duplicate the system-context diagram.",
    "Documentation links, SVG parsing, repository checks, full verification, and independent QA pass without including WI-0077 or WI-0079 changes."
  ],
